    "checks": [
      "Chapter 27 has no accessory dwelling text. C, RC, R-1, R-2 and R-3 permit single-family detached dwellings and customary accessory uses such as garages, playhouses, garden houses and pools (27-402, 27-502, 27-602, 27-702, 27-802)",
      "Residential conversions of an existing building are a permitted use in R-4 and MU-1: lot at least 8,000 sq ft and 65 ft wide, 2,000 sq ft of land and 700 sq ft of floor for each unit, no more than three units added, no exterior change, public water and sewer (27-902.5, 27-1402.4, 27-2009)",
      "More than one principal use may be built on a lot if each structure meets all lot and yard rules as though on its own lot (27-2110). On a nonconforming lot in a residential district only one single-family dwelling may be built (27-2203)",
      "District density caps: C 0.5 unit an acre, RC 1, R-1 2, R-2 4, R-3 8 units an acre. R-4 single-family 5 an acre (27-404 to 27-904)",
      "Accessory buildings: 15 ft high, not in the front yard, at least 10 ft behind the rear of the house, 3 ft from lot lines, 5 ft from an alley (27-2104.2, 27-2106.4)",
      "Parking: two spaces per dwelling unit (27-2302.1.E)",
      "Live-in caretaker or guard quarters are an accessory use in CH and IG only, not for homes"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Susquehanna Township (susquehannatwp.com). Read on eCode360 in a browser, the chapter print view searched in the page and section print views. Searched for accessory dwelling, accessory apartment, in-law, granny, elder cottage, ECHO, caretaker, guest house, carriage house, tenant house, second dwelling, tiny house, family suite, accessory residential, conversion, short-term. The only unlisted-use path is a special exception in IG for 'Any lawful use which the law requires the Township to provide for which is not otherwise permitted in any other district' (27-1303.5, 27-2047: 500 ft from any residential use). It does not reach a unit on a house lot."
